The '''1997 UEFA Cup Winners' Cup Final''' was a [[Association football|football]] match contested between [[FC Barcelona|Barcelona]] of [[Spain]] and the cup holders [[Paris Saint-Germain FC|Paris Saint-Germain]] of [[France]], to determine the winner of the [[1996–97 UEFA Cup Winners' Cup]] and the 37th overall [[UEFA Cup Winners' Cup|Cup Winners' Cup]] final. It was held at [[De Kuip]] in [[Rotterdam]] on 14 May 1997. Barcelona won the match 1–0 thanks to a [[Ronaldo (Brazilian footballer)|Ronaldo]] penalty. The final saw the last instance of the Cup Winners' Cup "jinx" that no club had successfully retained the cup in successive seasons — with Paris Saint-Germain failing to defend the trophy that they won in [[1996 UEFA Cup Winners' Cup Final|1996]].

